[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]Give your base room to grow[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5]Grow your base from its first upgrade to its last: [b]+100% radius[/b] by level 35 with the default settings. The Base Upgrade screen shows your current and next range, chest slots and Palbox boxes. Celebrate each expansion with a blue wave from the Palbox, a gentle bounce and a rising glow.[/size]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PikouGame/Growing-Grounds/999a446fffa9b154cb22e040a253101908e7cd89/assets/showcase/growing-grounds-upgrade-web.gif[/img][/center]

[size=5][i]Celebration captured in an earlier version, at original speed; initial wait trimmed.[/i][/size]

[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]More room for your supplies[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5]Chests gain [b]18 bonus slots[/b] by default, spread gradually across all base levels. Guild Chests receive the bonus once for their shared inventory. Open a chest to see its original capacity plus its extra slots above the grid.[/size]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PikouGame/Growing-Grounds/v0.2.0-beta/assets/showcase/growing-grounds-beta-chest.png[/img][/center]

[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]More boxes for your Pals[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5]Your regular Palbox gains [b]one extra box per base upgrade[/b], starting at level 2. The default cap is [b]32 extra boxes[/b], reached at level 33. The bonus follows your guild level once; extra bases do not multiply it. [b]Global Palbox storage is unchanged.[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PikouGame/Growing-Grounds/v0.2.0-beta/assets/showcase/growing-grounds-beta-palbox.png[/img][/center]

[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]Make it your own[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5]Three caps in [b]World Settings[/b], or in the dedicated-server config:
• [b]Range:[/b] 0 to +300%; default +100%, spread across all base levels and rounded to whole percentages.
• [b]Chest slots:[/b] 0 to 42 in steps of six; default 18. Slots still arrive gradually, one at a time.
• [b]Palbox boxes:[/b] 0 to 64 extra; default 32. One box per upgrade means level 35 can earn at most 34 extra boxes even with a higher cap.[/size]

[size=5]Set any cap to [b]0 (Off)[/b] to disable that bonus. Nearby bases can limit range growth. Lowering a storage cap keeps occupied extra slots or boxes until you empty them.[/size]

[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]Updating from 0.1.7 or earlier[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5][b]The new range curve can shrink existing bases.[/b] With the default cap, a level-11 base goes from 49 m to 45.2 m. Check buildings near the edge and back up before updating. Old chest caps round to the nearest multiple of six: 20 becomes 18, 40 becomes 42. Keep your config.lua and world-settings.ini.[/size]

[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]Getting started[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5]Install the complete mod on the [b]host/server and clients[/b], using your existing compatible [b]Palworld UE4SS loader[/b]. Update both sides together. Tested with Palworld 1.0.5.102999 and the UE4SS Palworld fork g2281fa31.[/size]

[size=5][b]0.2.0-beta:[/b] solo and dedicated-server tests passed through Proton/Wine. Testing this beta on a physical Windows/Steam installation is still pending.[/size]

[size=5][url=https://github.com/PikouGame/Growing-Grounds/blob/main/INSTALL.txt]Installation guide[/url] · [url=https://github.com/PikouGame/Growing-Grounds#testing-and-current-limits]Compatibility and known issues[/url][/size]

[size=6][color=#5cd5de][b]Share your experience[/b][/color][/size]

[size=5]We’d love to see what you build! Share your base, leave a comment, or [url=https://github.com/PikouGame/Growing-Grounds/issues]report a bug[/url] so we can keep improving Growing Grounds together.[/size]

[size=5][i]Made with OpenAI Codex and Claude under lelorax’s direction. Gameplay and UI captured in game. Free to use; all rights reserved for GG. Reuploads, published modifications and reuse require permission. Unofficial Palworld mod.[/i][/size]
